<Site title="About India Water Watch"><PageHeader title="About this project" eyebrow="Independent publication" description="India Water Watch is being built as a source-linked public information site about water across India." /><section class="section"><div class="shell page-grid"><article><h2>What the project is for</h2><p>The site is designed to help readers inspect measurements, their limits and the questions they raise. It treats conditions as something to investigate, not a prewritten national conclusion.</p><h2>How it is made</h2><p>Research and software work use AI assistance under an interactive editor-engineer lead. Agent review is recorded as agent review, not human approval. Current data and sensitive public claims require source, calculation and editorial checks before release.</p><h2>Corrections and contact</h2><p>A public correction channel has not been configured. Until then, no email address or contact form is represented as monitored. The release record will identify the publisher and contact route when configured.</p><p><a href={url('/corrections/')}>Correction record ↗</a></p></article><aside><p class="eyebrow">Publication controls</p><a href={url('/methodology/')}>Methodology</a><a href={url('/data-status/')}>Coverage</a><a href={url('/sources/')}>Sources</a></aside></div></section></Site>
